Subject: [PATCH] memory_tool: archival overflow hook

A memory provider may register a callback that accepts an entry exceeding the
curated char budget and files it into an unbounded, searchable tier instead of
rejecting the write. With no handler registered the behaviour is unchanged: the
at-capacity error is returned exactly as before.

Motivation: returning an error at capacity hands the model a dead end at the
precise moment it is trying to record something. Overflowing to a searchable
tier keeps the write and defers the curation decision.

Discovered 2026-07-25 as an uncommitted modification in the running checkout.

Verified to apply cleanly against a fresh clone of v2026.7.1.

